1
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,488
I understand the situation.

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:08,097
Now, I just have to explain
it to the rest of the guild.

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:11,709
Also, we'd like a temporary
leave of absence from the guild.

4
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:13,440
Really? Why?

5
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:19,026
We have concerns with the current state
of the guild, and we need time to think.

6
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:20,410
Very well.

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:27,454
Although, I'm positive you won't stay
away from the battlefield for long.

8
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,030
Wow!

9
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,440
This view is amazing!

10
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:51,157
It is pretty awesome, but
don't fall off the balcony.

11
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,593
That would really suck.

12
00:00:57,560 --> 00:00:59,340
We bought the best house.

13
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:02,280
And now we're totally broke.

14
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:06,773
It's worth it, though, because
we can live in peace here.

15
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:13,800
Kirito, what's wrong?

16
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:21,320
Well, I was thinking, does our
relationship only exist in this world?

17
00:01:21,540 --> 00:01:23,364
I can't believe you'd say that.

18
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:26,137
I don't give a damn if
this is a virtual world.

19
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,180
My feelings for you are real.

20
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:34,837
If I learned anything in the
last two years, it's this.

21
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:37,940
To keep doing the best
we can till the very end.

22
00:01:38,720 --> 00:01:43,037
And if we make it back to the real world,
I promise I'm going to find you again!

23
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:44,140
No matter what!

24
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:46,482
And fall in love with you again?

25
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,640
I'll see you later.

26
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,897
And I'm so glad that you're here.

27
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,804
Put a strong light in the dark.

28
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,597
I'll see my dreams in my heart.

29
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:14,297
I wanna always be with you.

30
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,200
I'll give you everything I have.

31
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:40,520
Usually he's brash and impulsive,
but he can be so naive, too.

32
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,680
Almost like a little kid.

33
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,920
Oh my god, is he younger than me?

34
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,010
Kirito.

35
00:03:58,460 --> 00:03:59,600
I love you.

36
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,627
Let's stay together forever.

37
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,080
Good morning, Kirito.

38
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,030
Morning.

39
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:19,200
D-did you hear what I said?

40
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:24,200
No, I didn't hear a thing. What'd
you say? Nothing! Not a thing!

41
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,149
Anyway, you want to go
have some fun today?

42
00:04:30,140 --> 00:04:33,140
Yeah, you know, didn't
we have fun yesterday?

43
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,220
And the day before, too?

44
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:42,416
So, you're saying you don't
want to go have fun today?

45
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:49,580
Wait, I know a place we can go. Come on.

46
00:04:55,440 --> 00:04:56,600
Where are we going?

47
00:04:57,220 --> 00:05:00,985
You're just going to have to wait
till we get there to find out.

48
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,540
Hey, carry me on your shoulders.

49
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,700
Seriously? Oh, please.

50
00:05:07,860 --> 00:05:10,977
It's no fun seeing the world from
the same height all the time.

51
00:05:11,060 --> 00:05:14,337
Besides, with your strength
parameter, you won't break a sweat.

52
00:05:14,420 --> 00:05:17,660
Yeah, I mean, I guess, but...

53
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,977
Aren't you a little old for that, though?

54
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:24,860
It doesn't matter how old I am. Come on.

55
00:05:25,060 --> 00:05:27,354
It's not like anyone's going to see us.

56
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:29,000
Okay, get on.

57
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,254
If you turn around, I'm gonna slap you.

58
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,776
Are you gonna hop on already or what?

59
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:42,970
Giddy up!

60
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:54,697
This is so cool, you can
already see the lake from here!

61
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,317
No, you can see the lake, I...

62
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:59,576
Okay, if you want, you can
ride on my shoulders later.

63
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:02,040
Let's get a move on, horsey.

64
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,880
We're heading north-northeast. Okay.

65
00:06:19,060 --> 00:06:20,589
It almost blew up my nose.

66
00:06:22,420 --> 00:06:24,440
We got people staring at us now.

67
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:26,700
Our own audience.

68
00:06:30,460 --> 00:06:33,200
Go on, read back or
he'll think you're rude.

69
00:06:33,380 --> 00:06:34,615
No, not gonna happen.

70
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,500
Do you want me to get off you now? Mama.

71
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,802
You're fine right where you are.

72
00:06:50,320 --> 00:06:53,157
I heard this weird rumor
in the village yesterday

73
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:56,240
About how if you go deep
enough into the forest,

74
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,360
you'll see... them.

75
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,100
See who?

76
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,510
Ghosts.

77
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:06,960
Y-you mean, like, those in-game
astral-type monsters, right?

78
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:08,740
No, not those.

79
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,980
Real ghosts.

80
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:14,997
They say the tortured souls
of the monsters hunted

81
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:18,480
here come back to wander
the forest at night.

82
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,640
We're almost there.

83
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:27,760
The place the rumor mentions?

84
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:33,680
About a week ago, a carpenter hiked into
the forest to get some wood for a project.

85
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:38,280
He stayed so long that before
he knew it, it was night.

86
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:43,400
As he walked along, he caught a glimpse
of something white standing by a tree.

87
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:52,900
Was it a monster?

88
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:54,540
Or something else.

89
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,660
The white figure slowly
walked towards some trees.

90
00:07:59,040 --> 00:07:59,940
Hey, look!

91
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,020
I want to get down!

92
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,258
I want to get down!

93
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,394
What's wrong with you?

94
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,030
It's...

95
00:08:19,113 --> 00:08:19,943
it's over there.

96
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:21,868
What are you talking about?

97
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,931
You've got to be kidding.

98
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,140
Hold on.

99
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:44,440
That's not a ghost.

100
00:08:45,100 --> 00:08:46,720
Wait, can't you?

101
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,960
Oh, jeez.

102
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,390
It's...

103
00:08:56,473 --> 00:08:57,303
another player!

104
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:01,240
Yeah, but there's something
really strange about her.

105
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:02,540
What do you mean?

106
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:04,349
She doesn't have a cursor.

107
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:09,927
Maybe it's some kind of bug.

108
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,760
Yeah, maybe it is.

109
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:15,800
What's a little girl like
this doing playing SAO?

110
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:21,692
I guess we'll find out when she wakes up.

111
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:24,657
But we can't just leave
her out here till she does.

112
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,387
Let's take her home with us.

113
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:27,800
Yeah, okay.

114
00:09:35,740 --> 00:09:37,257
Well, one thing's for sure.

115
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:38,537
She's not an NPC.

116
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:41,149
We didn't have any
trouble moving her here.

117
00:09:41,300 --> 00:09:42,860
Yeah, that's true.

118
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:45,360
She can't be that. If she were,

119
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:49,277
she would have given off a warning when
you picked her up, like other NPCs.

120
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,190
You're right.

121
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,066
And she's definitely not
a quest giver either.

122
00:09:53,460 --> 00:09:57,695
Our quest log would have been updated
as soon as we interacted with her.

123
00:09:58,300 --> 00:09:59,880
She has to be a player.

124
00:10:00,200 --> 00:10:04,057
She'd probably been out there for
a while, wandering around, lost.

125
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:06,022
That's the most likely scenario.

126
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:09,740
Yeah, but what was she doing out there?

127
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,245
Your guess is as good as mine.

128
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:15,197
But she has to have a parent
or guardian out there, right?

129
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:16,110
Mm-hmm.

130
00:10:16,193 --> 00:10:19,335
She had to have logged in
with someone from her family.

131
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,971
I just hope they're safe.

132
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:24,960
Hey, do you think she'll wake up?

133
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:26,610
Yeah.

134
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,217
If her body hasn't disappeared,

135
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:32,357
that means signals are still being
transmitted to and from her nerve gear.

136
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,381
She's in some kind of sleep mode.

137
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:36,940
I'm sure she'll wake up soon.

138
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:39,289
And the sooner the better.

139
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,390
Yeah.

140
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:50,060
Hey, Kirito?

141
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:11,820
I wonder, did she log into SAO by herself?

142
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,220
Or with her family?

143
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:17,320
Or has she been alone here all this time?

144
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,840
Sleep well.

145
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:28,240
Please hurry and wake up tomorrow.

146
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:47,400
Kirito! Wake up!

147
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:50,960
Good morning.

148
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,800
Something wrong? Hurry!

149
00:11:53,220 --> 00:11:54,060
Get over here!

150
00:11:58,420 --> 00:12:00,880
You woke up. Thank goodness.

151
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,736
Do you remember what happened to you?

152
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:09,950
Okay.

153
00:12:10,033 --> 00:12:11,680
How about your name?

154
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:14,870
My...

155
00:12:14,953 --> 00:12:16,420
my name is...

156
00:12:18,680 --> 00:12:25,560
I think my name is, I think,
Yui, Yui, that's it, Yui.

157
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:27,800
That's a cute name.

158
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:29,260
Nice to meet you.

159
00:12:29,560 --> 00:12:32,960
My name's Asuna, and this is Kirito.

160
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:36,860
Ahuna, Kirito?

161
00:12:38,260 --> 00:12:41,360
Try to remember, what were
you doing in the forest?

162
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:44,545
And do you know where
your mom and dad are now?

163
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:48,730
I…

164
00:12:48,813 --> 00:12:50,497
I don't know. I…

165
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:52,300
I can't remember anything.

166
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:54,320
Oh, no.

167
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:58,720
Well, you're awake.

168
00:13:00,720 --> 00:13:02,380
Can I call you, Yui?

169
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:03,890
Mm-hmm.

170
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,310
Okay.

171
00:13:05,393 --> 00:13:06,920
Then you can call me Kirito.

172
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,560
Can you say Kirito?

173
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,960
Cait?

174
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,017
It's Kirito.

175
00:13:13,100 --> 00:13:13,980
Kirito.

176
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:18,420
Thank you.

177
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,400
That's okay.

178
00:13:20,640 --> 00:13:22,111
Maybe it's a little hard.

179
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:25,184
How about you call me
whatever's easier for you?

180
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,190
Daddy.

181
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,790
Me?

182
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:34,480
Aona is… Mommy.

183
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:42,810
Okay.

184
00:13:42,893 --> 00:13:44,540
I'm Mommy. That works.

185
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:49,340
Mommy! Mommy! Daddy!

186
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:51,900
You must be hungry.

187
00:13:52,280 --> 00:13:53,477
Now, what about breakfast?

188
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,390
Okay.

189
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,340
Here you go, Yui. This one's yours.

190
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:11,360
Oh, I don't know, Yui.

191
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:12,893
This one's super spicy.

192
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:18,040
I want the same one that daddy has.

193
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,857
Okay, if you think you're
ready for it, I won't stop you!

194
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,880
You only live once, right?

195
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,097
I like it.

196
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:42,237
Wow, you've got an iron stomach!

197
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:46,085
We can do a full course of extra
spicy food tonight if you want.

198
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:49,117
Okay, let's not get carried away.

199
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:51,097
I'm not cooking anything nuclear.

200
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:52,298
You heard the lady.

201
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:53,698
You heard the lady?

202
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:07,080
So, what do you think?

203
00:15:07,940 --> 00:15:08,920
I don't know.

204
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,600
She's a blank slate.

205
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:11,820
No memories.

206
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,440
It's really weird.

207
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:14,960
Yeah, I know.

208
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:16,886
It's like she's a baby again.

209
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:18,177
I just...

210
00:15:18,260 --> 00:15:19,860
I don't...

211
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:22,540
I'm sorry.

212
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:24,332
I don't know what to do.

213
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:26,737
I get it.

214
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:28,457
You want to take care of her.

215
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:31,420
At least, until she gets her memory back.

216
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:33,257
Yeah, but...

217
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:34,740
But it's a catch-22.

218
00:15:35,340 --> 00:15:37,577
We have to get back and clear the game.

219
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:40,797
Otherwise, it'll take that much
longer for Yui to be free of it.

220
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:41,710
I know.

221
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:45,920
For now, we'll do what we can.

222
00:15:46,760 --> 00:15:51,701
Judging by the gear she's got in her storage,
she hasn't been out in the field much.

223
00:15:52,140 --> 00:15:54,117
We'll check the Town of Beginnings.

224
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:57,024
Maybe there we can find
out if she's got family.

225
00:15:58,040 --> 00:15:58,870
Okay.

226
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:02,344
Look, I don't want to say
goodbye to her either.

227
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:04,460
You really don't?

228
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,652
I don't know what it is.

229
00:16:07,280 --> 00:16:08,977
I mean, we just met her and all.

230
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:13,720
But having her here, it's made our
little cabin feel like a real home.

231
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,280
Don't you think so?

232
00:16:17,820 --> 00:16:20,408
This doesn't mean we'll
never see her again.

233
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:23,520
But look, if she's got a family out there,

234
00:16:23,740 --> 00:16:26,387
they're probably worried
about her right now.

235
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:30,849
Okay, when she wakes up, we'll
go to the Town of Beginnings.

236
00:16:31,180 --> 00:16:32,886
That place is army territory.

237
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:37,196
It might be a good idea if we go in
fully equipped, ready for anything.

238
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:39,228
Yeah, we better be careful.

239
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:40,870
Mommy.

240
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,670
Daddy.

241
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:53,340
It's been forever since
I've been back here. Me too.

242
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,200
What do you think?

243
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:04,713
Do any of these buildings look familiar?

244
00:17:07,620 --> 00:17:08,640
I don't know.

245
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:10,977
Don't get down about it.

246
00:17:11,060 --> 00:17:13,477
The Town of Beginnings
is a really big place.

247
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:14,640
So how about it?

248
00:17:14,780 --> 00:17:17,015
Should we start at the Central Market?

249
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:19,560
Hey, Kirito?

250
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:20,990
Yeah?

251
00:17:21,340 --> 00:17:23,157
Do you know how many players are here?

252
00:17:23,240 --> 00:17:24,534
Right now in the town.

253
00:17:25,780 --> 00:17:26,610
Hmm.

254
00:17:26,693 --> 00:17:27,523
Good question.

255
00:17:27,780 --> 00:17:31,320
Last I checked, there were 6,000
players still alive in SAO.

256
00:17:31,500 --> 00:17:35,717
And about 30 % of those people, including
the army, live in the Town of Beginnings.

257
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,520
So, maybe a little less than 2,000?

258
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:41,485
Then doesn't it seem a
little dead around here?

259
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:42,500
You're right.

260
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,920
Leave those children alone!

261
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:48,510
Look!

262
00:17:48,593 --> 00:17:49,900
It's that daycare bitch!

263
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:51,648
We've been waiting for you!

264
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:54,561
Leave them alone and let them go!

265
00:17:55,220 --> 00:17:58,877
You make it sound like we're doing
something illegal, babycakes.

266
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:01,537
We're just teaching them
how things work around here,

267
